---
title: Content collections
summary: RF-native content collections. One collection, two faces — data over the wire, bodies as components.
related:
  - content/markdown
  - content/live
  - content/blocks
---

`ogygia/content` gives SvelteKit content collections that fit the islands model. **This docs site is built on it** — every page you are reading is a `.svx` entry rendered through it.

> **When to use.** Reach for collections whenever you have a *set of content* with typed frontmatter — docs, a blog, a changelog, product pages — and you want a nav or index over the wire *and* full rendered bodies on the page. The [live sources](/docs/content/live) variant extends the same API to a CMS or an API feed.

One rule governs the whole surface: **the boundary picks the representation.** Stay on the server and you get the whole entry, body and all. Cross the wire and you get plain data.

| read | returns | where |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `get(id)` | `{ id, data, meta, body }` — body is a partial | server only |
| `list({ map })` | a mapped data array | over the wire |
| `live.get` / `live.list` | mapped data, re-emitted on change | over the wire (live) |

## Define the collection once

Put it in a plain module so both faces can reach it:

```ts
// src/lib/collections.ts
import { content, mdsvex } from 'ogygia/content';
import * as v from 'valibot';

export const docs = content({
  // `loader` is a source; `mdsvex()` wraps the glob. Data + Meta are inferred — no annotations.
  loader: mdsvex(import.meta.glob('../content/docs/**/*.svx', { eager: true })),
  schema: v.object({ title: v.string(), section: v.string() }),
  filter: (e) => !e.data.draft   // visibility, declared ONCE
});
```

`filter` is honored on every read path — `list`, `get`, `live`, and prerender inputs. A draft is invisible everywhere, including by direct URL. A per-remote filter can only narrow it further, never widen.

## Data for the wire: `list`

`list` and `live.list` mint real Kit remotes. Mint them in a `.remote.ts` (Kit requires every export there to be a remote); the consumer passes the args:

```ts
// src/lib/docs.remote.ts
import { withRemotes } from 'ogygia/content/server';
import { docs } from './collections';

export const docNav = withRemotes(docs).list({ map: (e) => ({ slug: e.id, title: e.data.title }) });
```

```svelte
<script>
  import { docNav } from '$lib/docs.remote';
  const nav = await docNav();
</script>
```

## An entry is `{ id, data, meta, body }`

`get(slug)` is server-only and returns the whole entry — `data` (validated frontmatter), `meta.headings` (for a TOC), and `body`, a [partial](/docs/data-state/partials) you render with `<Region>` — **or `null`** when the id is unknown or filtered out. `get` never throws; the caller decides the 404, so validate the slug in `load`:

```ts
// src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.ts — clean 404 for a missing entry
import { error } from '@sveltejs/kit';
import { docs } from '$lib/collections';

export async function load({ params }) {
  if (!(await docs.get(params.slug))) error(404, 'Not found');
}
```

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/docs/[...slug]/+page.svelte — load guaranteed it exists -->
<script>
  import { page } from '$app/state';
  import { Region } from 'ogygia';
  import { docs } from '$lib/collections';

  const entry = (await docs.get(page.params.slug))!;
</script>

<h1>{entry.data.title}</h1>
<Region of={entry.body} />   <!-- a demo island in the .svx hydrates here -->
```

Doing the 404 in `load` matters: `error()` maps to a real status from a load function, but thrown from the component's top-level `await` it escalates to a 500.

Prerender every entry from the route:

```ts
// +page.ts
export const prerender = true;
export const entries = async () => (await docs.ids()).map((slug) => ({ slug }));
```

## Rendering entries the client fetches

`get()` is server-only — the body is a live component, so it stays in the SSR pass. When the client needs to render an entry it fetched **over the wire** (an index, a live feed, search), map the entry to a partial of your own `with { region }` component and return that. `<Region>` fetches and hydrates it — see [Partials](/docs/data-state/partials).

See [Markdown & Shiki](/docs/content/markdown) for the preprocessor, and [Live & CMS sources](/docs/content/live) for `async` and streaming loaders.
